# Recipes for the {{PROJECT_NAME}} index

All commands accept `--root <project root>` and `--json`. Ids look like
`sym:<path>#<qualified.name>`, `doc:<path>`, `doc:<path>#<section>`, `file:<path>`.

## A. Find something by words

```
{{CMX}} q search "kalman gain" --limit 10
{{CMX}} q search "servo error" --kind section
```

Full-text over symbol names and docs, document titles and section text. Each hit has `cite`.

## B. Locate a symbol

```
{{CMX}} q find lookup_gain            # all symbols whose name contains it
{{CMX}} q symbol lookup_gain          # one symbol: signature, doc, callers, callees, documents
{{CMX}} q symbol "sym:matlab/lookup_gain.m#lookup_gain"
```

`q symbol` fails with the candidate list when a bare name is ambiguous; pick an id.

## C. Impact and call graph

```
{{CMX}} q callers gain_sched --depth 2
{{CMX}} q callees gain_sched --depth all
{{CMX}} q impact gain_sched
```

`impact` walks every hop with a seen-set and reports direct and total counts split by role
(`product`, `test`, `vendor`, `generated`, `docs`, `build`). It also lists `possible_callers`:
call sites that name the symbol but did not resolve. A symbol with no callers and no possible
callers may still be called dynamically; say "no mapped caller", never "dead".

## D. Files

```
{{CMX}} q file src/app/main.py
{{CMX}} q deps src/app/main.py            # what it depends on
{{CMX}} q deps src/app/util.py --reverse  # what depends on it
```

## E. Documents

```
{{CMX}} q docs "guide"                    # find by title or path
{{CMX}} q doc docs/guide.tex              # outline, references, symbols mentioned
{{CMX}} q outline docs/guide.tex
{{CMX}} q section "doc:docs/guide.tex#introduction" --text
{{CMX}} q refs docs/guide.tex             # links, cross-references, citations, paths
```

Section text comes from the extracted text cache. For anything load-bearing, open the
original file at the cited lines.

## E2. Terms, acronyms and named quantities

```
{{CMX}} q term "EKF"
{{CMX}} q term "gain scheduling"
{{CMX}} q param "servo error" --compare
{{CMX}} q param "" --value 50 --unit Hz
```

`q term` returns what the documents themselves say. Each hit carries `methods`: `acronym` (the
document wrote "Extended Kalman Filter (EKF)"), `defined` ("X is defined as ..."), `glossary`
(a glossary or nomenclature table row), `macro` (a LaTeX acronym macro), `heading` (a section
title used as a topic) and `keyphrase` (a statistical candidate from corpus TF-IDF). Quote a
definition only from the first four, and cite `defined_in`. Never present a keyphrase as a
concept of the document.

`q param` finds named quantities from spreadsheet cells (`source_kind: cell`), the numeric
literals inside their formulas (`formula-literal`) and quantities written in prose
(`prose`). A parameter's identity is its label, never its number. `--compare` groups by label
and returns `agree` or `differ` with the distinct values and where each came from; a `differ`
verdict is a finding, not an error. Values are read as stored, including hidden cells, so open
the cited cell or line before quoting a number.

## F. Relations and evidence

```
{{CMX}} q related "doc:docs/guide.tex#method"
{{CMX}} q explain "sym:matlab/run_all.m#(file)" "sym:matlab/gain_sched.m#gain_sched"
```

Every edge carries `rel`, `tier`, `confidence`, `evidence` and `status`
(`resolved`, `ambiguous`, `unresolved`, `external`).

## G. What is missing

```
{{CMX}} q skipped
{{CMX}} q skipped --reason grammar
{{CMX}} q status --json
```

`skipped` lists every file that was not fully analysed with a reason code:
`grammar-missing`, `missing-dependency`, `adapter-not-implemented`, `catalog-only`,
`binary-content`, `too-large`, `cloud-placeholder`, `extraction-failed`.

## H. Exact source

```
{{CMX}} q source src/app/util.py:1-12
{{CMX}} q source gain_sched --context 2
```

Returns the lines with a `cite` string; quote that string in the answer.
